@startuml
title Opening a second file while the first tab is dirty (T2)

actor User
participant "App::handle_key" as HK
participant "App::open_or_focus_tab" as Open
participant "tabs: Vec<OpenBuffer>" as Tabs
participant "ide_core::Buffer" as Buffer

User -> HK: Enter on a.txt (tree row)
HK -> Open: open_or_focus_tab(a.txt)
Open -> Tabs: any tab.path == a.txt?
Tabs --> Open: no
Open -> Buffer: Buffer::open(a.txt)
Buffer --> Open: Ok(buffer)
Open -> Tabs: push OpenBuffer { a.txt, ... }
Open -> Open: active_tab = Some(0)

User -> HK: Ctrl+T, type '!' (dirties tab 0)
HK -> Tabs: active_buffer_mut().buffer.mark_dirty()

User -> HK: Ctrl+T, Down, Enter on b.txt
HK -> Open: open_or_focus_tab(b.txt)
Open -> Tabs: any tab.path == b.txt?
Tabs --> Open: no
Open -> Buffer: Buffer::open(b.txt)
Buffer --> Open: Ok(buffer)
Open -> Tabs: push OpenBuffer { b.txt, ... }
Open -> Open: active_tab = Some(1)
note right of Tabs
  tab 0 (a.txt) untouched --
  still dirty, edit intact.
  T1 would have refused this
  whole step with a status message.
end note

User -> HK: Enter on a.txt again
HK -> Open: open_or_focus_tab(a.txt)
Open -> Tabs: any tab.path == a.txt?
Tabs --> Open: yes, index 0
Open -> Open: active_tab = Some(0)
note right of Open
  No Buffer::open call --
  the in-memory dirty edit
  is never re-read from disk.
end note
@enduml
